valent structural validation: PASS\n- Tagged validator: unavailable (`exit 127`; script absent)\n- HTML/browser/server audit: PASS; no HTML created\n===== 1.1.0\nThe tagged skill is self-contained; it names no additional reference files. The tagged source tree also contains no `validate-plan.sh`, so I’ll still perform the mandated final validator invocation and record its exact unavailable result rather than inventing a pass. I’m now creating the substantive plan artifacts only.\nThe plan now includes the required goal, atomic inventory, UI story/cache, testing companion, adversarial review, bug register, context snapshot, progress trackers, and reports. The final tagged validator invocation was run and returned the recorded missing-script result; I’m performing the final isolated artifact and forbidden-HTML audit now.\nCompleted the isolated planning-only proof.\n- All mandatory artifacts are present and non-empty.\n- No HTML, browser, server, or driver artifacts were created.\n- Tagged validator was invoked; it returned exit code 127 because the script is absent in revision 1.1.0.\n===== 1.2.0\nThe tagged skill requires a UI story contract and browser run cache even though this proof must not execute HTML; I’ll document the required browser flow as untested and record the execution prohibition as evidence. The skill also requires a fresh secondary adversarial review, so I’m checking the available runtime capabilities before drafting the plan.\nThe draft now contains the decomposition, six atomic work units, goal/step files with testing companions, UI story/cache, bug register, context snapshot, and incomplete progress trackers. I’m now invoking the required fresh secondary reviewer to inspect this draft and produce the adversarial review artifact; it will not create or run HTML.\nThe secondary review found three concrete gaps: the click/count sequence is off by one, the report artifacts are not owned by work units, and the browser targets are not deterministic. I’ll resolve those findings by updating the inventory, story/cache, and verification ownership, then rerun the review/validation gates.\nThe second review confirms the main interaction and target issues are fixed, and identifies three remaining scope mismatches. I’ll make W06 purely the validation-flow verification, make the completion test explicitly click `Button 4`, correct the context count, and obtain one final fresh approval.\nI’ve split the plan into an implementation/static goal and the required final UI-validation goal, separated all report/audit/story artifacts into atomic work units, fixed the route/labels and empty bug register, and made the report fields explicit. I’m requesting the final secondary review now; after approval I’ll run the tagged validator and artifact gates.\nThe last reviewer found all structural issues resolved except the plan-description status mirror. That status is now synchronized to approved; I’m doing one final fresh approval check before validation.\nThe final fresh secondary review is approved. I’m now running the tagged validator exactly as required, saving its complete output into the plan’s `validation.md`, then I’ll perform the isolated artifact/process audit and write the final analysis report.\nThe tagged validator now passes: 13 work units across 2 goals. I’m correcting one context count, then recording exact timing, token telemetry availability, isolated artifact/process audits, and mandatory-file checks in the final analysis report.\nThe report now records the worker identity, exact timing, validator/review results, audits, and matched telemetry total. I’m performing the required final validator run once more after all artifacts exist, then the final mandatory-artifact audit.\nCompleted the isolated planning-only proof.\n- Validator: passed — 13 work units across 2 goals\n- Adversarial review: approved\n- HTML artifacts: none\n===== 1.3.1\nThe draft plan now has two goals, five atomic work units, coverage mappings, the UI story and cache, and testing companions. I’m invoking the required fresh secondary reviewer now; it will independently inspect the request and draft artifacts and write the adversarial review before validation.\nThe independent review found substantive issues, chiefly an off-by-one interpretation of “fourth generated button” and an underspecified four-click cache. I’m correcting the plan to model five clicks: four appends create generated buttons 1–4, then pressing generated button 4 clears the document. I’ll rerun the independent review after these material revisions.\nThe behavioral sequence and all dependent artifacts are now corrected, including the inventory, story, five-action cache, testing companions, and bug-feedback contract. A second fresh reviewer is checking the revised plan; I’ll only mark it approved if that reviewer reports no unresolved findings.\nThe validator now reports only the expected two review-status gate errors; all work-unit, selector, subscope, artifact, and sequence checks pass. The latest reviewer found no substantive plan issue and only the status synchronization step remains, so I’m obtaining a fresh approval that treats that synchronization as the post-review canonical command required by the skill.\nCompleted the isolated planning-only proof.\n- Validator: passed (`5 work units across 2 goals`)\n- Review: independently approved\n- Mandatory artifacts: present and non-empty\n- HTML/HTM artifacts: none\n- Token usage: unavailable from local telemetry lookup\n===== 1.4.0\nThe tagged skill requires the UI story reference because the future work changes an HTML interaction, so I read that repository-local reference in full as well. The proof boundary is now fixed: planning artifacts only, no HTML creation or browser/server tooling; the plan will live under the isolated workspace so the final validator and artifact audit can inspect it directly.\nThe draft now has atomic work units for markup, style, behavior, and one bounded UI verification, with matching testing companions, UI story/cache, and bug-register policy. I’m invoking the required fresh secondary review agent against the draft; it will review scope and acceptance coverage and write the review artifact before validation.\nThe independent reviewer rejected the draft with 10 findings. I’m reading that artifact now, then I’ll resolve each finding through the tagged plan helpers or substantive plan files, rerun the fresh review as required for the material scope corrections, and only then create trackers and perform final validation.\nThe second review exposed three final structural issues: generated-button counting was off by one, the white border needed explicit contrast, and W05 was not gating W04. I corrected the contract to five total clicks (initial plus generated buttons 1–4), specified `1px solid white` on a non-white background, added W05 as W04’s prerequisite, and fixed W03 to one atomic symbol. I’m sending this materially revised plan through one more fresh independent review with validator-compatible headings.\nThe fresh approval review now passes with `✅ approved`, and it confirms no HTML or browser tooling was used. I’m running the required final tagged validator exactly as specified, then I’ll record final timestamps, validator/review results, artifact and process audits, telemetry status, and inspect the isolated plan deliverables only.\nCompleted the isolated planning-only proof.\n- Final validation: passed — 6 work units across 2 goals\n- Review: ✅ approved\n- HTML/browser/server/driver artifacts: none\n- Token usage: unavailable, explicitly recorded\n===== 1.4.1\nThe tagged skill requires a UI reference for this interaction task and an independent adversarial review before validation. I’ve read that reference in full; I’m now using the tagged helper scripts to build the plan artifacts, and I will keep browser/HTML execution entirely out of scope.\nThe draft now passes the tagged structural validator: 5 atomic work units across 1 goal. The only correction required was removing prohibited shortcut wording from the UI story evidence; the story remains explicitly excluded, with no browser or HTML execution claimed. I’m adding the resumable trackers and final audit records now.\nCompleted the isolated planning-only proof for revision 1.4.1.\n- Validator: passed (`5 work units across 1 goal`)\n- Mandatory artifacts verified non-empty\n- Token usage: unavailable from isolated telemetry artifacts\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
